            <div xml:id="d413">

                <pb facs="0406" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 437.00/42.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 153.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 21, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received Mr. Gibson’s
                    note No. 442 of the 26th ultimo, inclosing a copy of his note to the Cuban
                    Foreign Office, and a copy of that Office’s reply, in the matter of the
                    arbitration of the so-called “insurrectionary claims” against the Cuban
                    Government.</p>
                <p>The Department suggests that you advise the Secretary of State of Cuba that, in
                    view of the circumstances mentioned by him in his note, it would seem unwise at
                    this time to make public the expression of this Government’s opinion in favor of
                    arbitration of these claims. You may add however that this Government will be
                    glad to reconsider this determination as soon as the matter of submitting the
                    claims to arbitration again becomes urgent.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>(For <signed>Mr. Knox</signed>) <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
